 risen <strong class='sig'>+0.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.03 to +0.19), about +1.5\u00b0F since 1889.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 3 months fell. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Kansas City's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.22 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 39.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1961 (60.25 in); the driest, 1953 (20.93 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}